  "description": "UJAWEJ01 crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P -4 21 c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C148 H112 N12 O44 Pr8 Si1. From the CIF bond table, Pr1 (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr2 (Pr) has 6 O neighbors; Pr1A (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr2A (Pr) has 6 O neighbors; Pr1F (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr2F (Pr) has 6 O neighbors; Pr1G (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr2G (Pr) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.876-4.601 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 101.15-125.03°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Pr8L8(C6H4NH2COO)4SiO4] (C148H112N12O44Pr8Si).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
